{"name":"Chocolate Fountain","hex":"#9e5b40","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chocolate","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A food made from ground roasted cocoa beans.","A drink made by dissolving this food in boiling milk or water."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of or containing chocolate.","Having a dark reddish-brown colour/color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chocolate"},{"term":"fountain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A natural source of water; a spring.","An artificial, usually ornamental, water feature (usually in a garden or public place) consisting of one or more streams of water originating from a statue or other structure."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To flow or gush as if from a fountain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fountain"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chocolate fountain","blocks":[{"text":"A chocolate fountain is a device for serving chocolate fondue. Typical examples resemble a stepped cone, standing 2–4 feet (0.61–1.22 m) tall with a crown at the top and stacked tiers over a basin at the bottom. The basin is heated to keep the chocolate in a warm liquid state so it can be pulled into a center cylinder then vertically transported to the top of the fountain by an Archimedes screw. From there it flows over the tiers creating a chocolate \"waterfall\" in which food items typically like marshmallows, cookies, strawberries or other fruits can be dipped by using a skewers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Small_Chocolate_Fountain.JPG/330px-Small_Chocolate_Fountain.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate_fountain"},{"title":"Chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"Chocolate is a food made from roasted and ground cocoa beans. It can be a liquid, solid, or paste. It is eaten on its own and used to flavor other foods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg/330px-Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate"},{"title":"Fountain","blocks":[{"text":"A fountain, from the Latin \"fons\", meaning source or spring, is a decorative reservoir used for discharging water. It is also a structure that jets water into the air for a decorative or dramatic effect in landscapes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Fountains_Collage.jpg/330px-Fountains_Collage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fountain"},{"title":"Chocolate (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The color chocolate or cocoa brown is a shade of brown that resembles chocolate. At right is displayed the color traditionally called chocolate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Chocolate02.jpg/330px-Chocolate02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Chocolate_fountain.jpg/120px-Chocolate_fountain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Chocolate_fountain.jpg/250px-Chocolate_fountain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Chocolate_fountain.jpg/120px-Chocolate_fountain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChocolate_fountain.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Woman-using-chocolate-fountain.jpg/120px-Woman-using-chocolate-fountain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, 